6d577407-a819-5ca6-9183-79b25b7e9329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054418 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13031" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054418 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x,$ if $-\\dfrac{3}{4}x = 12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054418 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d0477ef-8561-5404-b97a-99a49031c4ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054418 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides by $\\color{blue}4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) & =4\\cdot 12 \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{\\cancel{4}}x) & =48 \\\\ -3x & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by ${\\color{red}-3}$ to isolate $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =48 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3} & =\\frac{48}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}} & =-16 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054419 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054419 #edb/ref 1071 "If $-\\dfrac{3}{2}t = 24$, then what is the value of $t?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054419 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9acb3bf7-12c7-51db-a8a6-30111c3b7e86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054419 #edb/ref 1074 "We multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $-\\dfrac{3}{2},$ which is \n\n$$\n\\left( -\\dfrac{3}{2} \\right)^{-1} = -\\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}t & =24 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}t) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 24 \\\\ 1t & =-\\frac{2}{\\cancel{3}}\\cdot \\cancel{3}\\cdot 8 \\\\ t & =-16.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054420 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054420 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 = -8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054420 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64b6a66a-c061-52e2-a3aa-e54b7542715c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054420 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the fractional term $\\dfrac{3x}{4}$ by adding $5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \t\t\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 &=-8\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5+5 &=-8+5\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4}+0 &=-3 \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4} &=-3\n\t}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $\\dfrac{3}{4},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal $\\left( \\dfrac{3}{4} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{3}{4}x &=-3 \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{4}x &= \\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot (-3) \\[5pt]\n1 x &= - \\dfrac{4}{\\cancel{3} } \\cdot \\cancel{3} \\[5pt]\nx &= -4.\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186486382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054792 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186486353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186486459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving One-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054793 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "08568384-d6f2-503a-98f7-fa3f5052caa1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054794 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218605